// Musa is total: every function has to finish, and the way one earns that is
// to recurse on a piece a `match` took out of its own argument. `sequence`
// counts down in the *body* — `steps` never gets smaller in the call — so
// nothing here descends, and a sequence over zero steps would still ask for
// one more. The fix is to match on `steps` and recurse on the piece the
// `Succ` arm hands back.
piece "A Recursion With No Measure" {
    fn sequence_up(steps: Nat, from: Nat) -> Nat {
        sequence_up(steps, from + 1)
    }

    score {
        part solo {
            voice line {
                c4/1
            }
        }
    }
}
